// A field-level rule (spec §6.2): `$` is the value being checked. Here, a
// referential-integrity check — the value must be the id of a real Customer.
// The host says this is a field rule and what `$` holds (`rule.fieldType` and
// `fieldValue` in the config, or `--field` on the command line).
//
//   minab run customer-exists.minab
//   minab run customer-exists.minab --trace   # the one parameterized EXISTS
//
// The fixture answers "yes" whatever `$` is; against a real database
// (`--database`), `--field '"c-404"'` would come back `false`.

EXISTS(#Customer[.id == $])
